# [Landing Party Rosters](landing_rosters)

The bridge crew of the ship that answers the call - and, when the call takes them down
to the surface, the landing party as well. You go down as the person you have been all
evening rather than as a stranger off a list, so this file is the cast for both.
`landing_party.amd` still holds the hand-authored bodies, used when nobody is manning
the consoles at all.

`Roles:` is what an away scene GUARDS on - `if security`, `if medical`. A post without
one falls back to the console it names, so Reyes at science satisfies `if science` and
Kovac at engineering satisfies `if engineering` with nothing written here. Only a job
whose name is not its seat needs saying out loud, which is why weapons carries
`security` and nothing carries `medical`: this watch has no medic, and the medic's
lines are forwarded to whoever is covering rather than lost.

Kept in its own file on purpose. `crew_load_amd` parses with `amd_crew_data` and the
story content is read with `amd_mission_data`; one file read by two parsers is a trap.

